# Spec lock before WRITE

Do not implement an unchecked epic/story until spec_lock has run.

1. Read `.agents/gaps/spec-lock.md` and execute every section.
2. Cross-check `project_tasks_implementation_plan.md`, `ZVec.NET-RAG-project-plan.md`, `README.md`, and `docs/**`.
3. Invoke `zvec-gap-detection-expert` with trigger `spec_lock` (plus architect, rag-pipeline, docs, vectordata, native-aot as the checklist assigns).
4. If any P1 spec contradiction, or an open `D-*` for the epic being started is not tasked: **amend docs/plans first**. Do not start WRITE.
5. Record new spec findings as `S-*` in `.agents/gaps/registry.md`.

Gap detection after a commit is not a substitute. Consultants compare plan vs plan vs engine vs wiki; agents must do the same before code.
